{
  "intro": [
    {
      "text": "Beings of Roshar named for the things they gather around. There are said to be thousands of kinds, from the size of a thumbnail to bigger than buildings.",
      "revealedIn": [{ "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "49" }]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fragments of the powers of creation that gained awareness through the influence of thinking beings on Roshar. They vary hugely in look and intelligence. A Nahel bond with a spren lets Knights Radiant Surgebind.",
      "revealedIn": [
        {
          "all": [
            { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "57" },
            { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "3" },
            { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "33" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "description": [],
  "history": [],
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "Characteristics",
      "items": [],
      "parts": [
        {
          "title": [
            {
              "text": "What spren are",
              "revealedIn": [
                { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "49" },
                {
                  "all": [
                    { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "48" },
                    { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "99" }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "There are said to be thousands of kinds of spren, each named for the thing it gathers around. The smallest are the size of a thumbnail; the largest dwarf buildings.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "49" }]
            },
            {
              "text": "Rosharans call many beings spren, including Shards and Cognitive Shadows. Objects have Cognitive aspects, also called spren, that look like beads in Shadesmar and can be bribed with Stormlight; this is how Soulcasting works.",
              "revealedIn": [
                {
                  "all": [
                    { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "48" },
                    { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "99" }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": [
            {
              "text": "How they behave",
              "revealedIn": [
                {
                  "all": [
                    { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "i-5" },
                    { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "45" }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "all": [
                    { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "i-5" },
                    { "book": "rhythm-of-war", "chapter": "44" }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Lesser spren are said to be always present, though often unseen, and appear around their namesake. Even common kinds sometimes fail to show. All spren are very rare in Shinovar, and emotion spren are rare in crowds.",
              "revealedIn": [
                {
                  "all": [
                    { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "i-5" },
                    { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "45" }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "Larger spren can change shape, copy faces and voices, and pick up small objects. Some Unkalaki, called alaii'iku, can see spren that do not show themselves.",
              "revealedIn": [
                {
                  "all": [
                    { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "i-5" },
                    { "book": "rhythm-of-war", "chapter": "44" }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": [
            {
              "text": "Death",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "84" }]
            }
          ],
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "A Radiant's spren can die if the Radiant breaks their oaths badly enough. Before the Radiant has a Shardblade, the spren only seems to fade away, and it can return if the Radiant keeps the oaths and swears them again.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "84" }]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Classification",
      "items": [],
      "parts": [
        {
          "title": [
            {
              "text": "Lesser spren",
              "revealedIn": [
                {
                  "all": [
                    { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "17" },
                    { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "4" }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Most spren are lesser spren, also called subspren, and are not sapient. Some can speak, but talking with them rarely gets anywhere. Spren of the same kind are essentially the same as one another.",
              "revealedIn": [
                {
                  "all": [
                    { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "17" },
                    { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "4" }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": [
            {
              "text": "True spren",
              "revealedIn": [
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "4" },
                { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "i-9" }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Sapient spren are called true spren. Each seems to stand for a higher idea, such as honor for honorspren or truth and lies for Cryptics.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "4" }]
            },
            {
              "text": "True spren that cross into the Physical Realm can barely affect it. In Shadesmar most are human-sized and humanlike; in the Physical Realm they take smaller, simpler forms.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "i-9" }]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": [
            {
              "text": "Unique spren",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "104" }]
            }
          ],
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "A few spren are one of a kind, such as the Nightwatcher, the Stormfather, the Sibling and the nine Unmade. Each has its own power, and their minds range from nearly human to animal-like.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "104" }]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": [
            {
              "text": "Odium's spren",
              "revealedIn": [
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "i-7" },
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "i-3" }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Voidspren are made of Odium's essence. Lesser voidspren are not sapient but can bond singers to give them Regal forms.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "i-7" }]
            },
            {
              "text": "Some voidspren are sapient. Unlike other true spren, they keep their minds in the Physical Realm without a bond. They usually look like small Shin people, coloured yellow or red.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "i-3" }]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Bonds",
      "items": [],
      "parts": [
        {
          "title": [
            {
              "text": "Bonds with animals",
              "revealedIn": [
                {
                  "all": [
                    { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "i-5" },
                    { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "26" }
                  ]
                },
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "99" }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Ryshadium horses have evolved to draw a spren, most likely musicspren, which may explain their intelligence and strength.",
              "revealedIn": [
                {
                  "all": [
                    { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "i-5" },
                    { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "26" }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "Greatshells use spren bonds to grow far larger than they otherwise could: an unknown spren in their gemhearts, and mandras, which lessen gravity. Skyeels bond mandras to fly without wings.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "99" }]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": [
            {
              "text": "Singer forms",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "79" }]
            }
          ],
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Singers change form by taking a spren into their gemheart during a highstorm. Each form has its own shape and biology: warform is tall and armoured, and only some forms can have children.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "79" }]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": [
            {
              "text": "The Nahel bond",
              "revealedIn": [
                {
                  "all": [
                    { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "57" },
                    { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "120" }
                  ]
                },
                { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "86" },
                {
                  "all": [
                    { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "52" },
                    { "book": "rhythm-of-war", "chapter": "110" }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "A spren bonded to a person through the Nahel bond keeps its full mind in the Physical Realm, and its partner can Surgebind.",
              "revealedIn": [
                {
                  "all": [
                    { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "57" },
                    { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "120" }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "A Knight Radiant strengthens their bond by speaking Ideals. Once it is strong enough, the spren can become a Shardblade of any shape the Knight needs, and speak to them in their mind.",
              "revealedIn": [{ "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "86" }]
            },
            {
              "text": "Each kind of Radiant spren has lesser spren cousins, which form a Radiant's Shardplate once they reach a high enough Ideal.",
              "revealedIn": [
                {
                  "all": [
                    { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "52" },
                    { "book": "rhythm-of-war", "chapter": "110" }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": [
            {
              "text": "Unique spren",
              "revealedIn": [
                {
                  "all": [
                    { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "89" },
                    { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "95" }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Some unique spren can be bonded. Bondsmiths draw their powers from such bonds, and the Stormfather is one of three great Bondsmith spren. Some Unmade bond people too.",
              "revealedIn": [
                {
                  "all": [
                    { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "89" },
                    { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "95" }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Enlightened spren",
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "The Unmade Sja-anat can corrupt lesser spren, which she calls Enlightening. Enlightened spren look misshapen, with parts painfully exaggerated.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "97" }]
        },
        {
          "text": "Enlightened lesser spren can spy and carry messages for Sja-anat, speaking in her voice into the mind of the person they are sent to.",
          "revealedIn": [
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "4" },
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "97" }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Sja-anat can now Enlighten true spren too. They can still form Nahel bonds, and Enlightening does not force them to side with Odium.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "117" }]
        },
        {
          "text": "Sja-anat calls the spren she has Enlightened her children.",
          "revealedIn": [
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "85" },
                { "book": "rhythm-of-war", "chapter": "i-2" }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "parts": []
    },
    {
      "title": "Myths and lore",
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "Rural Vorin folk believe in malicious spren such as raspings, stormwhispers and, most feared, nightspren. Educated people think the Knights Radiant made these up long ago.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "42" }]
        },
        {
          "text": "Vorin teaching calls the Dawnsingers spren sent by the Almighty to care for humanity, bringing gifts such as the Dawnchant. They turn out to be the ancient singers, not spren.",
          "revealedIn": [
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "54" },
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "11" }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Folklore calls the Voidbringers evil spren with bodies of stone that eat human flesh. The tales draw on Odium's servants, and the truth comes out that the Voidbringers were humans.",
          "revealedIn": [
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "45" },
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "111" }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "parts": []
    }
  ],
  "facts": [],
  "people": [
    {
      "characterId": "stormfather",
      "role": "Bondsmith spren",
      "revealedIn": [
        {
          "all": [
            { "book": "words-of-radiance", "chapter": "89" },
            { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "95" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
